Footprinting and Reconnaissance Using Kali Linux

Project Overview

This repository documents a practical cybersecurity internship exercise on Footprinting and Reconnaissance using Kali Linux.

The project focuses on gathering publicly available information about a target domain using six different command-line tools.

Target Domain: networkwalks.com

Objectives

- Retrieve public domain registration information.
- Identify website technologies and frameworks.
- Resolve domain names into IP addresses.
- Analyse HTTP response headers.
- Detect Web Application Firewall (WAF) protection.
- Enumerate publicly available DNS records.

Tools and Commands

Tool| Command| Purpose
WHOIS| "whois networkwalks.com"| Domain registration lookup
WhatWeb| "whatweb networkwalks.com"| Technology fingerprinting
NSLOOKUP| "nslookup networkwalks.com"| DNS resolution
CURL| "curl -I https://networkwalks.com"| HTTP header analysis
WAFW00F| "wafw00f networkwalks.com"| WAF detection
DNSRECON| "dnsrecon -d networkwalks.com"| DNS enumeration

Skills Practised

- Footprinting and reconnaissance.
- Domain information gathering.
- DNS analysis.
- Website technology identification.
- HTTP header inspection.
- Basic web security assessment.
- Kali Linux command-line operations.

Learning Outcomes

This exercise provided practical exposure to reconnaissance techniques and demonstrated how different Kali Linux tools can be used to gather information about a website's publicly accessible infrastructure.
